.TH PORTCHECK 1 "October 26, 2026" "homebrew-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
portcheck \- show which process listens on a TCP port, and stop it safely
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B portcheck
[\fB\-j\fR]
[\fB\-k\fR [\fB\-f\fR] [\fB\-t\fR \fISECS\fR] [\fB\-n\fR] [\fB\-y\fR]]
.I PORT
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B portcheck
asks
.BR lsof (8)
for the processes listening on TCP
.I PORT
and prints their PID, command, owner and bound addresses.
It is read\-only unless
.B \-\-kill
is given.
.PP
Stopping a process sends SIGTERM, waits, and only escalates to SIGKILL with
.BR \-\-force .
PID 1, launchd, the calling shell and processes owned by another user (unless
running as root) are never signalled.
Without a terminal, a stop requires
.BR \-\-yes .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Print the listeners as JSON.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-kill
Stop the listening process(es) with SIGTERM after confirmation.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
With \-\-kill, send SIGKILL if the process survives SIGTERM.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout " " \fISECS\fR
Seconds to wait after SIGTERM. Default 5.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the signals that would be sent, and send none.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Do not ask for confirmation.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A listener was found, and stopped when \-\-kill was given.
.TP
.B 1
Nothing listens on the port.
.TP
.B 2
The process could not be stopped.
.TP
.B 64
Usage error.
.TP
.B 69
lsof is not available.
.TP
.B 77
Refused: protected process, another user's process, or no confirmation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
portcheck 3000
portcheck \-\-json 5432 | jq '.listeners[].pid'
portcheck \-\-kill \-\-dry\-run \-\-force 8080
portcheck \-\-kill 8080
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lsof (8),
.BR kill (1)
